## 11. Summary

The proposed framework establishes a practical way to evaluate the
complete solution as documents are added incrementally:

``` mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Source Documents<br/>~1,400"] --> B["Batch Ingestion"]
    B --> C["Knowledge Graph"]
    B --> D["Vector Database"]
    C --> E["Entity Enrichment Classification"]
    E --> F["High / Average / Poor"]
    F --> G["Golden Questions"]
    G --> H["KG-based Provisional Baseline"]
    G --> I["Vector Retrieval Tests"]
    G --> J["RAG Answer Tests"]
    H --> K["Quality Evaluation"]
    I --> K
    J --> K
    K --> L["Six Primary KPIs"]
    L --> M["Quality Reports / Dashboard"]
    M --> N["Regression, Enrichment and Repeatability"]
    N --> O["Next Document Batch"]
    O --> B
```

This framework is intended to answer five core questions:

1.  Are entities being enriched as expected?
2.  Does the Vector Database retrieve relevant supporting information?
3.  Does RAG provide accurate, complete, evidence-based answers?
4.  Does the system abstain appropriately when information is missing,
    particularly for poorly enriched entities?
5.  Does quality remain stable as new document batches are ingested?

**Recommendation:** Retain this as **Version 1.0 -- Discussion Draft**.
Review the architecture assumptions, ownership, golden-question
approach, and KPI definitions with the relevant teams. Once agreed,
convert it into the formal System Testing Strategy and detailed Test
Plan. The priority is to establish a reliable, measurable baseline
quickly and enhance the framework only when the evidence or project
needs justify it.